WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
This is the brief on Georgia's booming film industry.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Imagine finding out your backyard is secretly the coolest movie set in the world.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Well, Georgia is now the Hollywood of the South,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
hosting blockbusters like Marvel's Avengers and hit shows like Stranger Things.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
First, why are huge movies moving to Georgia?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
It's a massive discount.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Georgia gives productions an uncapped 30% tax credit.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Think of it like a giant store coupon.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
If they spend $500,000 and slap that Georgia Peach logo in the credits, they save a ton.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Now, you might wonder why would a state hand out millions like a coupon?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Well, to build massive things and make even more money.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Second, where does this movie magic happen?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Thanks to that mega discount, gigantic studios popped up.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
The biggest is Trilith Studios, just south of Atlanta.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
It's a massive 700-acre complex, literally the biggest outside Hollywood.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
With 34 sound stages, it's basically a real-life mini-city

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
with a town, houses, and a school.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.000
It was the actual home base for hits like Spider-Man: No Way Home and Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Finally, what's the real-world impact?

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
That coupon strategy totally worked.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Movies bring billions to local Georgia businesses for catering and hotels,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
supporting roughly 60,000 jobs.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Despite a recent slowdown from Hollywood strikes and rising costs, Georgia isn't giving up.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Starting in 2026, they're offering a brand-new 30% discount

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.000
specifically for post-production work like sound and editing.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.000
So, while Hollywood might be the historic home of cinema,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Georgia's smart discounts and massive studio cities

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
prove the Peach State is a modern movie-making superpower.